      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63f122e2_ee5ab6ee",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 7055,
      "author": {
        "id": 1086611
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-08T20:31:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about this. The challenge here is how to enable Wifi network selector to obtain this information. I prefer not to have network selector to call WifiNative to get these values by itself. Also I try to avoid passing them around as input parameters. \n\nFor device configuration parameters we can access them from context.getResources(). Seems like we are lack of ways to access the configurations generated on the fly. \n\nAn alternative I thought of is to add two APIs in WifiStateMachine for network selector to get this max blacklist and whitelist sizes. Just like how network selector checks if firmware roaming is supported.",
      "parentUuid": "8b193853_88b9fe01",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7055,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 7055,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "21e02eaf79bdcf8ea9e22307364116636ca0bf05",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f0cf8c8_93ed7c2b",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 7079,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-08T00:17:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks like it has a potential for race conditions with resets since this is sending a separate message.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7079,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 7079,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "21e02eaf79bdcf8ea9e22307364116636ca0bf05",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bec9b781_62c2fa3d",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/WifiStateMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 7079,
      "author": {
        "id": 1086611
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-08T20:31:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you mean resetFirmwareRoamingConfigurations() by \u0027reset\u0027 here? That\u0027s invoked in the CMD_START_CONNECT message. Can you elaborate more why you think sending a separate CONFIGURE_FW_ROAMING message would have race condition?\n\nActually while going through the code again, I think there is a bug with the configuration reset logic in CL. If a blacklist is created because of association rejection, it will be cleared by the very next CMD_START_CONNECT attempt even if the target network has the same SSID as the previous failed attempt, which defeats the purpose of this blacklist. The reset should be moved to the network disconnection handling. But this is not a race condition.",
      "parentUuid": "9f0cf8c8_93ed7c2b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7079,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 7079,
        "endChar": 44
      },
